translation.jira.listingIdentity.personal	your Atlassian account
translation.jira.loadingStatuses	Loading statuses…
translation.jira.noProjects	No Jira projects
translation.jira.noProjectsMappedTooltip	No Jira projects available for this org. Check that Devin's Jira account can see the project and, for enterprise orgs, that it is mapped to this org in Jira connection settings.
translation.jira.noStatuses	No Jira statuses
translation.jira.noStatusesFound	No statuses found
translation.jira.projectsError.saSiteAccessRevoked	Jira rejected the service account entirely — its access to the Jira site appears to have been revoked (often by an access-expiry or identity-governance policy). Ask a Jira admin to re-grant the service account product access to the site, and to exempt it from any automatic access-revocation policy so this doesn't recur.
translation.jira.projectsError.saNoPermission	The Jira service account can't see any projects. Make sure it has the Browse projects permission and the read:jira-work scope in Jira, then try again.
translation.jira.projectsError.adminNoPermission	The connected Jira account can't see any projects. Make sure it has the Browse projects permission and the read:jira-work scope in Jira, or reconnect Jira with an account that has access.
translation.jira.projectsError.connectRequired	Connect your Atlassian account to load Jira projects.
translation.jira.projectsError.notConnected	Jira integration not found. Reconnect Jira to manage project mappings.
translation.jira.projectsError.tokenRefreshFailed	Jira authentication failed and the token could not be refreshed. Reconnect Jira to restore access.
translation.jira.projectsError.agentTokenUnavailable	The Devin app for Jira hasn't checked in yet, so projects can't be listed. Try again in a few minutes.
translation.jira.projectsError.rateLimited	Jira is rate limiting requests to this site, so projects can't be listed right now. Try again in a few minutes.
translation.jira.projectsError.generic	Couldn't load projects from Jira.
